R-C10 R-TG1 R-TG3 R-C4 R-SP19 R-EC10 R-AL8 (slice 054, OP10): the release of a platform has the build target. The platform pf has 3 releases: 0.1.0 and 0.1.1 have the targets x64musl and wasm32, 0.1.2 has x64musl only. Run 1 (`[build] target = "wasm32"`, the header has pf 0.1.0, `update`): pf is free and moves, but 0.1.2 is no candidate, so it moves to 0.1.1 (the build is `--target=wasm32`). Run 2 (no `[build]`): rule 2 of R-TG1 takes the target from the release, so 0.1.2 is a candidate, and the build is `--target=x64musl`. Run 3 (`install` with no names holds the platform: R-SP19; the header has pf 0.1.2 and `[build] target = "wasm32"`): no tuple exists, exit 10, no probe, nothing written (the answer OP10 of the user: exit 10, not 2). Run 4 (`update`, the platform hpf has only x64musl in both releases): no release is a candidate, exit 10. Run 5 (gap test C3, `pf = "acme/pf@=0.1.2"`, `[build] target = "wasm32"`): the one candidate has no wasm32, but the release of the header has it, so a platform release passes the gate: the failure keeps the text of the solver, and `no_release` is not used. The text of the failure is a proposal (TW24).
